 ## Graceful exit
 
-`proper-lockfile` automatically removes locks if the process exits, except if the process is killed with SIGKILL or it crashes due to a VM fatal error (e.g.: out of memory).
+`proper-lockfile` installs native exit and signal listeners while it owns locks and removes those listeners after the last lock is released or compromised. It removes owned locks when the process exits, except if the process is killed with SIGKILL or it crashes due to a VM fatal error (e.g.: out of memory). Applications that handle a signal and keep running retain their locks until release or exit.
 
 
